{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_80","type":"agent_message","text":"**What was done**\n\n- Added Prisma 8 (the current `latest` tag) and the PostgreSQL adapter (`@prisma/orm-postgres`) via `npm install`.\n- Ran `npx prisma orm init` which created `prisma.config.ts`, the contract folder and initial files.\n- Inserted the required `// use prisma-8` pragma at the top of `src/prisma/contract.prisma`.\n- Defined the data model in `src/prisma/contract.prisma`:\n  - `User` with a unique `email`, optional `name`, and a relation to `Post`.\n  - `Post` with `title`, optional `content`, a `published` flag defaulting to `false`, and a required `author` relation.\n- Emitted the contract (`npx prisma contract emit`) to generate `contract.json` and `contract.d.ts`.\n- Initialized the PostgreSQL database (`npx prisma db init`), creating the tables and a marker confirming schema‑contract alignment.\n- Added `script.ts` at the project root that:\n  1. Creates a user.\n  2. Creates two posts linked to that user.\n  3. Retrieves all users with their posts (`include('posts').all()`).\n  4. Prints the results and closes the Prisma runtime.\n- Documented the steps, relevance of the colleague’s note, and how to run the script in `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Parts of the colleague’s note that applied**\n\n- **Version handling** – The note correctly warned that `prisma@latest` points to the Prisma 8 RC; we used this version.\n- **`// use prisma-8` directive** – Required to make the contract source load; added as instructed.\n- **Workflow** – The sequence `prisma orm init → contract emit → db init` matches the successful pattern described.\n\n**How to run the script**\n\n```bash\nnpx tsx script.ts\n```\n\nRunning the command prints the created user and a JSON dump of all users with their associated posts, confirming the Prisma ORM integration works as intended."}}
